# PokeEngmon core

- Sensitive values (diamonds, entries, exp, candies) go through Supabase RPC wrappers in `js/supabase-auth.js`. Logged-in RPC failure must **not** silently fall back to local fake success.
- plpgsql: prefix vars `v_`, params `p_`; qualify columns with aliases.
- Capture: always pass **stage1** dex to `obtainCapture` / `settleCapture`.
- `EVOLUTION_CHAINS` is an array — use `.find(c => c.key === …)`, never `EVOLUTION_CHAINS[key]`.
- Audio prefs live in `pokeengmon_audio_v1` (not cleared by progress reset).
- PowerShell: no `&&`; prefer Python for UTF-8 file edits. Use `python tools/git_commit_push.py --paths …` when the user asks to commit/push.
- Layout / responsive (red frame, safe-area, sheets, display-window overlays, modals/toasts, breakpoints, rotate prompts, touch targets): read `.trae/skills/pokeengmon-responsive/SKILL.md` first — it is the single source. New rules go only inside `@media (min-width: 700px)`+; 440×956 must not regress; verify with a browser preview + console. Do NOT run `tools/responsive/` tests / `npm run test:e2e` unless the user explicitly asks (slow, token-heavy).
- Before any code/SQL/UI/release change: read only the index table at the top of `.trae/skills/pokeengmon-preop-checklist/SKILL.md` (first ~25 lines), then Grep the matching topic skill(s) under `.trae/skills/pokeengmon-*/` for the relevant Rules/keywords — don't read whole skill files unless the change is large.
